        "created_at": "2011-11-06T22:15:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Right now, there are two types of ways to “multiply” damage.  There is “for each” and there is “times x”.  The ones written as “for each” are considered separate attacks, and are buffed indivicually, whereas ones written as multiplied deal a single attack.  Though today I heard Chris say something about something written in some rulebook to some expansion to some game that is supposed to make an easier and more consistant ruling for this issue.  But until then, what awp832 said (in this case).</p>",
